From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team <oe.patch@openatv.example>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GLES: force the GLES2 renderer path on Vu+ Zero 4K

Kodi requests an EGL_CONTEXT_CLIENT_VERSION 2 context on the STB windowing
backend and is built with OPENGLES_FORCE_GLES2.  The BCM72604 V3D driver still
reports "OpenGL ES 3.1" through GL_VERSION.  Kodi consequently selects its
GLES 3.1 shaders and texture handling at runtime, which corrupts the color and
alpha composition of GUI images while the separate font path remains intact.

Keep the actual driver string in the graphics log, but expose GLES 2.0 to
Kodi's renderer selection on the affected receiver.  Other Vu+ receivers and
hardware video composition remain unchanged.

diff --git a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
--- a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@ bool CRenderSystemGLES::InitRenderSystem()
       sscanf(ver, "%*s %*s %d.%d", &m_RenderVersionMajor, &m_RenderVersionMinor);
     m_RenderVersion = ver;
   }
+#if defined(TARGET_VUZERO4K)
+  if (m_RenderVersionMajor >= 3)
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+              "Vu+ Zero 4K GLES compatibility: driver reports {}, forcing Kodi's GLES 2.0 "
+              "renderer path",
+              m_RenderVersion);
+    m_RenderVersionMajor = 2;
+    m_RenderVersionMinor = 0;
+  }
+#endif
 
   // Get our driver vendor and renderer
   const char *tmpVendor = (const char*) glGetString(GL_VENDOR);
-- 
